      "message": "fix(ui): the tool window's next number skips reserved pockets; the full-probe refusal says what to do\n\nThe tool window compared a new tool's typed number with a next free\nnumber that ignores the machine's reserved pockets. With T1 reserved for\na probe, a typed 1 queued nothing and the cutter became T2 with no\nmessage. The window now uses tool_numbers::next_free_for, the same\nallocation as AddTool, so a typed 1 goes to SetToolNumber and is refused\nby name.\n\nWhen each reserved probe pocket holds a tool, the refusal now names the\npockets and tells the user to delete or renumber a tool there, or to\nreserve one more probe pocket. Refusals name a tool_setter reservation\nas \"tool setter\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nFixes #3667",
